---
title: Vindaloo
source: https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2018/feb/08/how-to-cook-the-perfect-vindaloo-recipe
servings: 6
course: Main
locale: en
difficulty: Medium
cuisine: Indian
---

= Masala Marinade =

Grind together all the ingredients for the masala (@Kashmiri chilli or paprika{2%tbsp}, @cardamom pods{8}(seeds only), @black peppercorns{1%tsp}, @cloves{8}, @cumin seeds{1%tsp}, @coriander seeds{0.5%tsp}, @turmeric{0.5%tsp}, and @cinnamon{1%tbsp}), then stir in the @cider vinegar{75%ml}.

Rub into the @beef shin, pork shoulder, or duck breast{700%g}(cut into 3 cm chunks) and leave to marinade for 3 to ~{4%hours}.

= Vindaloo =

Heat the @ghee or sunflower oil{4%tbsp} in a wide, lidded pan over a medium-low heat, and fry the @onions{4%medium}(finely sliced) until soft and golden.

Stir the @garlic{10%cloves}(finely sliced) and @ginger{5%cm}(cut into slim matchsticks) into the onions and cook, stirring, for another ~{5%minutes}. Add the @ripe tomatoes{4}(diced), @bird eye green chillies{4}, and @curry leaves{10}. Cook until the tomatoes start to break down.

Add the meat and marinade to the pan. Increase the heat to medium high. Stir well, add the @soft brown sugar{1%tbsp}, @salt{1%tsp}, @mustard seeds{1%tsp}, and @tamarind sauce{60%g}. Bring to a simmer, then reduce to a low heat. Cover and cook gently for ~{1%hour}.

Remove the lid and cook for another ~{30%minutes}, until the meat is very tender and the sauce has thickened.